    "priority": 58,
    "degree": "n=2*p^r+sum_(a=1)^t c_a*p^(k_a)+d*p^j",
    "domain": "Any finite t>=0; p odd prime; r>k1>...>kt>j>=2, every consecutive gap>=2; even 2<=c_a<p; odd 1<=d<p; s>r; every characteristic-zero primitive p^s phase q.",
    "conclusion": "Both original P_n and H_n are squarefree; original ordinary algebraic-square Christoffel-Darboux kernel is nonzero at every original P_n root.",
    "incremental_credit": "Only t>=2 after subtracting every inherited high-order, fixed-node and successful residual certificate. t=0 and t=1 retain prior credit; two-middle proof/review are dependencies, not separately added discoveries. Exact C_u subtraction remains in the proof.",
    "proof_boundary": "Arbitrary-prefix monic covers, not an assumed prefix-simplicity theorem; actual immediate neighbors/shift errors/off-root derivative terms, every boundary and intervening annulus are handled. Algebraic squares are not absolute-value squares.",
